The good linear log-log plots of response vs. concentration, shown in Figure 4b, are consistent with typical chemiresistive behavior. The theoretical limit of detection (LOD) was calculated to be ${\sim}0.02$ ppm using the linear log-log plot and ${\sim}0.35$ ppm using the linear plot by setting response $\mathbf{\tau}=\mathbf{\tau}$ 3RMS (RMS $\mathbf{\tau}=\mathbf{\tau}$ rootmean-square deviation).[12a, 18] These values are comparable with the best LOD values of RT chemiresistors reported to date (Table S4). When compared with common interfering gases, such as ethanol and acetone, the sensor also showed good selectivity toward $N H_{3}$ (Figure 4b, S16 and S17). The good selectivity toward $N H_{3}$ might be due to the strong gas-framework interaction, as revealed by the IR peaks of $N H_{3}-C u^{+}$ and $N H_{3}$ - $\mathsf{C u}^{2+}$ , and the resulting red shift of $\mathsf{\upsilon}_{\mathsf{U}}(\mathsf{C}_{\mathsf{-}}\mathsf{O})$ (Figure 4c).[19] This can be further confirmed by the lattice expansion observed upon $N H_{3}$ adsorption, based on PXRD patterns (Figure 4d). Such expansion was not observed with $\mathsf{O}_{2}$ because there are only weak interactions between $\mathsf{O}_{2}$ and the framework (Figure S18).
In summary, a new 2D π-conjugated dual-ligand based ECMOF, $\mathsf{C u}_{3}(\mathsf{H H T P})(\mathsf{T H Q}).$ , was synthesized via a simple solutionphase method. This EC-MOF possessed a unique trigonal crystal structure and modulated conductivity. The obtained crystalline black powders of $\mathsf{C u}_{3}(\mathsf{H H T P})(\mathsf{T H Q})$ nanowires indicated a trigonal unit cell $(\mathsf{P3}\mathsf{m}\mathsf{1})$ with cell parameters of $\mathsf{a}=$ $\mathsf{b}=17.154\mathrm{~\AA~}$ , and $\mathsf{c}=6.266\mathsf{A}$ in an AB slightly slipped-parallel stacking mode. The products not only showed modulated conductivity $({\sim}2.53\times10^{-5}\lor\subset\mathsf{m}^{-1})$ and semiconductive behaviors with a thermal activation energy of $0.30~\mathsf{e V},$ , but also exhibited high porosity $(\sim441.2\ \mathsf{m}^{2}\ \mathsf{g}^{-1})$ . The $\mathsf{C u}_{3}(\mathsf{H H T P})(\mathsf{T H Q})$ nanowires thick film sensor exhibited good discrimination toward low concentrations of $N H_{3}$ with an excellent LOD, down to $0.02-$ 0.35 ppm. The dual-ligand based EC-MOFs provided a new design for the modulation of electronic conductivity and porosity. We trust this work will inspire more dual or multi-ligand based EC-MOFs containing unique combinations organic ligands with different sizes, shapes, or functional groups for the discovery of new functional materials.
